prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a timed obstacle-course game. Load the animated Fox.glb model and use keyboard controls to guide the fox through 10 obstacles (alternating hurdles and tunnels).

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/Fox.glb;
(2) Fox.glb contains animations (such as Survey, Walk, Run, etc.); use AnimationMixer to manage the animations;
(3) After loading is complete, place the fox at the starting position and scale it appropriately (the Fox model is relatively large and may need to be scaled to 0.01-0.02 times its original size);
(4) After loading is complete, set window.__3D_STATE__.modelLoaded = true;

[Course Construction]
(5) Create a straight course approximately 100 units long, with brown/green ground laid out using PlaneGeometry;
(6) Place 10 obstacles at equal intervals along the course. Odd-numbered positions (1,3,5,7,9) are hurdles (to be jumped over), and even-numbered positions (2,4,6,8,10) are tunnels (automatically crouch to pass through);
(7) Hurdles: transverse BoxGeometry bars approximately at the fox's waist height (Y=0.5), identified with red-and-white striped colors;
(8) Tunnels: semicircular arches or rectangular door frames assembled from BoxGeometry, with a low height that forces crouching, identified in blue;

[Control System]
(9) Arrow Up / Down (or W / S): control the fox's forward/backward movement; play the Run animation while moving;
(10) Spacebar: jump, with the fox's Y coordinate rising and then falling along a parabola (jump height approximately 1.5, duration approximately 0.6 seconds); play a corresponding jump animation or use the Survey animation;
(11) Automatically crouch when approaching a tunnel obstacle (scale the Y axis to 0.5 times its normal size), and restore it after passing through;
(12) Play the Survey (idle) animation while the fox is stationary;

[Collision Detection]
(13) Use simple AABB bounding-box collision detection;
(14) Hitting a hurdle (when not jumping) or the top of a tunnel (when not crouching) counts as a collision:
  a) On collision, increment window.__3D_STATE__.collisions++;
  b) On collision, add a 2-second time penalty;
  c) On collision, make the obstacle flash red for 0.5 seconds;

[Timing System]
(15) Start the timer when the fox moves for the first time;
(16) Stop the timer when the fox passes the final obstacle;
(17) Final time = actual elapsed time + collision penalty time (number of collisions × 2 seconds);

[Camera]
(18) Use a third-person follow camera positioned behind and above the fox, always looking at the fox and following its movement;

[HUD Display]
(19) Display the following in a HUD panel in the upper-left corner:
  - Timer (id="timer", format MM:SS.ms);
  - Number of obstacles cleared (id="obstaclesCleared");
  - Number of collisions (id="collisionCount");
  - Current speed (id="speed");
  - Model loading status (id="loadStatus");

[Visual Effects]
(20) Use a light-blue sky as the scene background (0x87ceeb);
(21) DirectionalLight (sunlight) + AmbientLight;
(22) Simple trees or fence decorations may be added along both sides of the course;

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean (whether the model has finished loading)
  - timer: number (current elapsed time in seconds)
  - obstaclesCleared: number (number of obstacles cleared, 0-10)
  - collisions: number (number of collisions)
  - speed: number (current movement speed)
  - foxPosition: {x, y, z} (the fox's current position)
  - isJumping: boolean (whether the fox is currently jumping)
  - gameStarted: boolean (whether the game has started)
  - gameFinished: boolean (whether the course has been completed)

Output a single HTML file. Place this file in the same directory as the assets/ folder and run it through a local HTTP server.
